IMPORT `cpp-core`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- INTERPRETATION (regulation 37).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 417 to 427.
--
-- Regulation 37 defines three terms for Part V and prescribes four things for the Act. "The Minister" in Part V is the
-- Minister of Employment and Social Development (see the core's `Minister`). The Income Tax Act and the Act's own
-- definitions of "federal institution" (section 104(1), piece cp6) are not among the texts this encoding reads, so
-- what they decide is taken as a plain input and said so beside the input.

§ `Part V -- Interpretation (regulation 37)`

§§ `37(1) -- Canada child benefit`

-- src:420 | 37 (1) In this Part,
-- src:421 | Canada child benefit means the deemed overpayment determined in accordance with section 122.61 of the Income Tax Act in respect of a qualified dependant under seven years of age; (allocation canadienne pour enfants)
@ref Reg 37(1) "Canada child benefit" (src:421)
GIVEN `the amount is the deemed overpayment determined under section 122.61 of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: the Income Tax Act is not deposited
      `the amount is in respect of a qualified dependant under seven years of age` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 37(1) — an amount is a Canada child benefit`
    `the amount is the deemed overpayment determined under section 122.61 of the Income Tax Act`
    `the amount is in respect of a qualified dependant under seven years of age` MEANS
    `the amount is the deemed overpayment determined under section 122.61 of the Income Tax Act`
        AND `the amount is in respect of a qualified dependant under seven years of age`

§§ `37(1) -- personal representative`

-- src:424 | personal representative means the executor, administrator, heir or other person having the ownership or control of property comprised in the estate of a deceased person or, where there is no estate, the survivor of the deceased person or, where there is no such survivor, the next of kin of the deceased person. (représentant personnel)
@ref Reg 37(1) "personal representative" (src:424)
GIVEN `there is an estate of the deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the executor, administrator or heir of the estate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has the ownership or control of property comprised in the estate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a survivor of the deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN   -- "survivor" is defined in section 42(1) of the Act (piece cp3)
      `the person is the survivor of the deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the next of kin of the deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 37(1) — a person is the personal representative of a deceased person`
    `there is an estate of the deceased person`
    `the person is the executor, administrator or heir of the estate`
    `the person has the ownership or control of property comprised in the estate`
    `there is a survivor of the deceased person`
    `the person is the survivor of the deceased person`
    `the person is the next of kin of the deceased person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is an estate of the deceased person`
           THEN (`the person is the executor, administrator or heir of the estate`
                 OR `the person has the ownership or control of property comprised in the estate`)
        IF `there is a survivor of the deceased person` THEN `the person is the survivor of the deceased person`
        OTHERWISE `the person is the next of kin of the deceased person`

§§ `37(2) and (3) -- persons and agencies authorized to receive a benefit under regulation 57`

-- src:425 | (2) For the purposes of subsection 60(2) of the Act, a person entitled to make an application includes a person or agency authorized to receive a benefit under section 57 of these Regulations.
-- src:426 | (3) For the purposes of subsection 60(4) of the Act, a person entitled to receive benefits includes a person or agency authorized to receive a benefit under section 57 of these Regulations.
@ref Reg 37(2) (src:425)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to make an application under subsection 60(2) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 60(2) (piece cp5)
      `the person or agency is authorized to receive a benefit under section 57 of these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN   -- decided by regulation 57 (cr2-payment-of-benefits.l4)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 37(2) — a person is entitled to make an application for the purposes of subsection 60(2) of the Act`
    `the person is entitled to make an application under subsection 60(2) of the Act`
    `the person or agency is authorized to receive a benefit under section 57 of these Regulations` MEANS
    `the person is entitled to make an application under subsection 60(2) of the Act`
        OR `the person or agency is authorized to receive a benefit under section 57 of these Regulations`

@ref Reg 37(3) (src:426)
GIVEN `the person is entitled to receive benefits under subsection 60(4) of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 60(4) (piece cp5)
      `the person or agency is authorized to receive a benefit under section 57 of these Regulations` IS A BOOLEAN   -- decided by regulation 57 (cr2-payment-of-benefits.l4)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 37(3) — a person is entitled to receive benefits for the purposes of subsection 60(4) of the Act`
    `the person is entitled to receive benefits under subsection 60(4) of the Act`
    `the person or agency is authorized to receive a benefit under section 57 of these Regulations` MEANS
    `the person is entitled to receive benefits under subsection 60(4) of the Act`
        OR `the person or agency is authorized to receive a benefit under section 57 of these Regulations`

§§ `37(4) -- the prescribed individual who is a public officer`

-- src:427 | (4) For the purpose of the definition public officer in subsection 104(1) of the Act, a prescribed individual is a person employed in a federal institution or whose services are required by a federal institution, on a casual or temporary basis or under a student employment program.
@ref Reg 37(4) (src:427)
GIVEN `the individual is employed in a federal institution` IS A BOOLEAN   -- "federal institution" is defined in section 104(1) of the Act (piece cp6)
      `the individual's services are required by a federal institution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is so employed or required on a casual or temporary basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the individual is so employed or required under a student employment program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 37(4) — an individual is a prescribed individual for the definition public officer in subsection 104(1) of the Act`
    `the individual is employed in a federal institution`
    `the individual's services are required by a federal institution`
    `the individual is so employed or required on a casual or temporary basis`
    `the individual is so employed or required under a student employment program` MEANS
    (`the individual is employed in a federal institution` OR `the individual's services are required by a federal institution`)
        AND (`the individual is so employed or required on a casual or temporary basis`
             OR `the individual is so employed or required under a student employment program`)
